Most scripts here are from the EMRG tidal model:
https://github.com/EnvModellingGroup/tidal_model_template

There are several scripts for this work, which are:
create_ocean_parcels_vel.sh
generate_start_positions.py
ocean_parcels_connectivity.py
calc_intersections.py
create_connections.py
create_connectivity_matrix.py

They should be run in that order. 

create_ocean_parcels_vel.sh <- creates the netcdf rasters from h5 files from thetis output. Set resolution etc.
generate_starts_positions.py <- write 2 CSV files for all starting positions. Ensures determinisitic particle runs
ocean_parcels_connectivity.py <- runs the parcels code and generates trajectories. Run in parallel, even if just 2 cores or the rest may not work!
calc_intersections <- calculates intersection points with the reef polygon file. Each intersection is stored.
create_connections <- create the connectivity bones of a connectivity matric based on a competancy curve for a coral species using data from Randall et al and an expoential death model. Run once per species.
create_connectivity_matrix.py <- make the connectivity matrix from the connections.

You then have a connectivity matrix (or two, or three...) for each species of coral across the whole GBR.


